# ---- clip v2 (item 164): the video bank scene's VideoSurface, played on the surface itself - the
# game draws it. The typed find is find_node + 0x2f4; the surface's functions sit at layout B's
# distances from surface_state (aerosmith_le-1.15), each prologue equal to it. A clip was seen on the glass in
# the emulator 2026-09-25 (item 164).
site surface_find     0x0046d4b0 0xe92d4070 0xe24dd008
site surface_set_video 0x00464d44 0xe5d03238 0xe92d4ff0
site surface_play     0x004624e4 0xe5d03238 0xe92d43f0
site surface_stop     0x00461fe8 0xe5d03238 0xe92d40f0
# PAD-725: the surface's own seek, length and position (PAD-530's, from Bond 1.06): a mode's clip the game's own
# clip took the surface from comes back where it would be by then. Placed by the James Bond LE 1.06 recipe at
# its distances from surface_play (+0x1bc / -0x1274 / -0x360: the older player), each proven by its call: the
# player's virtual seek (+0x20), duration (+0x28) and position (+0x24), whose entries call gst_element_seek /
# query_duration / query_position.
site surface_seek     0x004626a0 0xe92d43f0 0xe1a07003
site surface_duration 0x00461270 0xe5d03238 0xe92d40f0
site surface_position 0x00462184 0xe5d03238 0xe92d40f0
# PAD-725: the game's reel (a clip of its own kept in step with a song): its tick waits while a clip of
# ours has the bank's surface. Found by what it calls (surface_position, surface_seek, surface_play) and
# its prologue (push; mov r4, r0; ldr r0, [r0, #0x1c]; cmp r0, #0; popeq).
site reel_tick       0x002a1de0 0xe92d47f0 0xe1a04000
# PAD-725: the backdrop on the bank's surface, as Bond's (PAD-521): a mode's loop plays there again whenever it
# is idle, and a clip the game loops there gets one pass before the loop takes it back. Emulator-proven on the
# newest build of every title with a clip v2 bank, 2026-10-25.
value backdrop_surface 1
value surface_playing       2

